// One glyph row of the loaded face, read back through the real offset
// formula (txt_glyph_at) rather than a hand-computed index -- so this stays
// correct however tall a loaded face's cell is. Code point 65 ('A'), row 2:
// the built-in face's top two rows of a capital letter are blank, and this is
// the first row with any ink, so it distinguishes a real table from a zeroed
// one.

txt_glyph_arow() {
  int off = txt_glyph_at(65);
  int v = (import txt_glyphs)[off + 2];
} return int v;
